    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to introduce to the market No.18 Wadelai Road, a fantastic three bedroom family home with an east facing rear garden. This property offers spacious, light-filled accommodation, coupled with some lovely original features, and is sure to appeal to discerning buyers looking to establish a home within easy reach of Dublin city centre. The property requires full modernisation but offers tremendous potential to create a fantastic family home.\n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 159 sq m and comprises a large porch, entrance hallway, spacious living room, dining room, kitchen/breakfast room, second living area, large utility room, fourth bedroom, and downstairs wc. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms and a family bathroom. The property benefits from gas fired radiator central heating and a large driveway to the front, providing ample off street parking.\n\nAlongside its convenient setting, the property is situated just 5km from Dublin city centre. Dublin Airport is within a 10-minute drive, while the M50 is approximately 2km to the north. Excellent local amenities include the National Botanic Gardens, with a range of primary and secondary schools also within easy reach. DCU is just a 10-minute walk away. The area is well serviced by public transport, with Dublin Bus routes providing convenient access to the city and surrounding areas.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the spacious accommodation, excellent location and wonderful family home has to offer.\n\nContact DNG Estate Agents in Phibsboro.\nLocal DNG agents: Isabel O'Neill, Brian McGee, Vincent Mullen, Leah Barry, Michelle Keeley & Ciaran Jones MIPAV"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 1.71m x 5.36m\nBright entrance porch with tiled flooring, timber surround and an abundance of natural light.\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.78m x 3.97m\nInviting entrance hallway with carpet flooring, wallpapered walls and access to the downstairs wc\n\nReception Room - 4.96m x 2.99m\nLarge living room situated to the front of the property, featuring carpet flooring, wallpapered walls and a decorative fireplace surround. Double doors provide access to the dining area.\n\nDining Room - 3.76m x 3.20m\nDining room situated to the rear of the property, featuring a decorative fireplace with gas insert and painted walls.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 3.59m x 5.14m\nLarge, spacious kitchen/breakfast room with an abundance of wall and floor units, providing ample storage, and access to a large utility room.\n\nUtility Room - 3.67m x 3.10m\nLarge utility room with additional storage and a dedicated sink area featuring a Belfast sink\n\nLiving Room - 3.08m x 5.36m\nFeaturing a combination of lino and carpet flooring, wallpapered walls and a fireplace surround.\n\nDownstairs wc - 1.78m x 1.25m\nFully tiled downstairs bathroom comprising wc, wash hand basin and hotpress.\n\nLanding - 1.80m x 3.23m\nLanding area with carpet flooring and wallpaper décor\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.07m x 2.99m\nLarge dual aspect double bedroom with carpet flooring, built in fitted wardrobes and painted decor.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.17m x 3.09m\nSituated to the rear of the property, quality fitted lino flooring and painted decor.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.17m x 2.25m\nSituated to the rear of the property, this versatile single room would make an ideal child's bedroom.\n\nBedroom 4/Home office - 5.23m x 3.10m\nThis room would make an ideal fourth bedroom or home office, featuring laminate wood flooring and ample storage space - access via utility room\n\nBathroom - 1.80m x 2.11m\nFully tiled family bathroom comprising wc, wash hand basin with vanity unit and Jacuzzi bath.\n\nOutside front - \nLarge cobbled driveway providing ample off street parking for a number of vehicles.\n\nOutside rear - \nEast facing, low maintenance paved rear garden, enclosed by a combination of wall and fencing.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Year of constuction 1947</li><li> East facing rear garden</li><li> Gas Heating</li><li> Two Bathrooms</li><li> Large utility room</li><li> Large private driveway with ample off street parking</li><li> Walking distance to local schools, DCU, Botanic gardens, bus routes, shops and sports facilities</li><li> Close to M50, Dublin Airport and City Centre</ul>"
      },
